WEBVTT

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.420
Every government meeting leaves a record.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:04.210
So, here's the question.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.940
Who else is holding a copy?

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.020
Let's talk about it.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.430
Because clouds get breached.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:10.800
In 2023,

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.430
it was sixty thousand State
Department emails.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:14.720
A year later,

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.030
the US Treasury, through one
of its vendors.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.590
StenoAI works differently.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.440
Run it on the Apple silicon Macs
you already have,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.530
on an M6 mini we set up for you,

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.970
or on NVIDIA DGX Spark.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:27.790
Your call.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.240
Put it in the room,

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.150
and it quietly writes the minutes
as people talk.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.710
Those minutes stay right there,

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:36.860
on the box,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.520
until you decide to share them.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:39.650
No network.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.440
No vendor in the middle.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.210
Nothing sitting in a cloud,
waiting to leak.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.500
And when the meeting's over,

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.830
the box leaves with you.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:48.740
It's open source,

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.180
so your own team can check every line.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.650
And it's built around GDPR, data
residency and records law.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.120
Now compare the usual options.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.490
Tools that live on public cloud.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:03.010
Suites that can't promise sovereignty.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.880
Or a server room you'd have to build
and staff yourself.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.390
StenoAI is open to audit,

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.100
backed by a contract,

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.360
and it sits on one box you own.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.750
For enterprise teams, we add
a hardened build,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.450
custom workflows and real support,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.940
from the first briefing
to full deployment.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:23.700
StenoAI.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:24.790
Your minutes.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:25.950
Your custody.
